omxplorer, a desktop spreadsheet app for data scientists (1440x900), showing a 1,000,000-row CSV of orders. Layout top to bottom:
1. Title bar: the app name "omxplorer" in lowercase on the left, the document name "orders.csv — 1,000,000 rows" centred, a Share and a Save button on the right.
2. Toolbar of icon-above-label buttons in groups separated by thin vertical lines: [Open, Save, Undo, Redo] [Table, Chart, Pivot, Formula, Add row] [Sort, Filter] then on the far right [Format]. Chart is hovered.
3. Formula bar: a cell reference box "J12", an "fx" label, the input "= revenue - cost", cancel and accept buttons.
4. The main area: a data grid filling the width, with a row-number gutter (1 to 24 visible) and columns order_id, date, region, customer, product, carrier, qty, revenue, cost, margin. Each column header has its name, a small type badge (# for numbers, $ for money, Aa for text, a calendar for dates) and a tiny distribution histogram under the name. Realistic rows: dates like 2026-07-14, regions West/East/North/South/Central, products like Desk Chair, Monitor Arm, carriers UPS/FedEx/DHL, revenue like $1,284.50. Column "margin" is a formula column. Column "revenue" is selected (header tinted, cells tinted), cell J12 has the selection ring. A row of totals at the bottom of the grid.
5. Right inspector panel 300px with tabs "Format · Column · Table", Format active: section NUMBER with a segmented control (Auto, Number, Currency, Percent), Currency chosen; decimals stepper (2); a "Thousands separator" switch on; negatives choice (-1,234.00 or (1,234.00)); currency symbol dropdown ($). Section COLUMN STATS: count 1,000,000, empty 0, distinct 812,441, min $4.20, max $9,980.00, mean $72.06, and a small histogram.
6. Bottom bar, left: sheet tabs "Orders" (active), "Report", and a + button. Right: status figures "Sum $72,061,236.00 · Average $72.06 · Count 1,000,000 · GPU RTX 4090 · 0.3 ms".
Dense, precise, numbers right-aligned in a monospace font.
